<title>FINLAND: ASKO PROPOSES FIVE-FOR-ONE SHARE SPLIT.</title>
<headline>ASKO PROPOSES FIVE-FOR-ONE SHARE SPLIT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish plastic pipes, white goods and furniture maker Asko Oy said on Tuesday it would propose a five-for-one share split to the annual general meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;The board of directors will propose to the shareholders meeting on March 25, 1997 ... (that) the nominal value of the share should be 10.00 markka instead of the current 50.00 markka,&quot; Asko said in a statement with its 1996 results.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope this will increase liquidity,&quot; Asko CEO Jarmo Rytilahti told a news conference.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
